            <ArticleTitle>Circular Photoinduced Electron Transfer in a Donor-Acceptor-Acceptor Triad.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>841-845</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201708207</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An electron-donor-acceptor-acceptor (D-A1 -A2 ) triad has been developed that provides the first proof-of-concept for a photoinitiated molecular circuit. After photoexcitation into an optical charge-transfer transition between D and A1 , subsequent thermal electron-transfer from A1.- to A2 is followed by geometric rearrangement in the D.+ -A1 -A2.- charge-separated state to form an ion-pair contact. This facilitates &quot;forward&quot; charge recombination between A2.- and D.+ to complete the molecular circuit with an estimated quantum efficiency of 4 % in toluene at 298 K.</AbstractText>
